on and optional details so downstream issue aggregation can preserve complete incomplete-signal context. The workflow framework will treat this as a failure signal even when the agent exits successfully.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"details":{"description":"Optional extended details or diagnostic context about the failure (max 65000 characters).","maxLength":65536,"type":"string"},"reason":{"description":"A concise explanation of why the task could not be completed (max 1024 characters). Be specific about which tools or resources were unavailable.","type":"string"}},"required":["reason"],"type":"object"},"name":"report_incomplete"},{"description":"Custom safe-job: create_report_incomplete_issue","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":true,"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"create_report_incomplete_issue"}]}}}
agent	Parse MCP Gateway logs for step summary	2026-08-24T01:12:07.8928829Z {"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:11:59.611Z","event":"rpc_request","_schema":"rpc-message/v2","direction":"OUT","server_id":"safeoutputs","method":"tools/call","payload":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"tools/call","params":{"arguments":{"body":"Adds `docs/plans/orbprp.md`, a modernization plan for the `ORBPRP` subroutine (`legacy/src/geosat.f:522-591`), which computes the quick-look subsatellite point archived via the fixed-column `REPORT` output.\n\nThe plan documents:\n1. Current behaviour cited to line numbers.\n2. Preserved defects — most notably the single-precision `DT` time-overflow truncation that causes frames a few seconds apart to propagate to identical subsatellite points, and the fact that `SSALT` is never actually propagated (always the frozen element constant). Both are load-bearing for the archive and are recommended to be pinned as tests, not fixed.\n3. Coverage gaps in the existing golden vectors (no vector exercises the longitude-wrap boundary, the single-precision collapse boundary, or an `ARGLAT` wrap across multiple orbital periods) with concrete descriptions of the new vectors needed.\n4. An ordered, independently revertible set of characterization-only steps (add golden vectors → add modern unit assertions → register vectors in the parity harness → document defects in comments), each with a named proof obligation (a specific test, not \"verify correctness\").\n5. Explicit scope boundaries — no change to `ORBPRP`'s arithmetic, `geosat.inc` layout, or `REPORT` format statements.\n6. Open questions for a human decision-maker regarding the two preserved defects and the frozen element set.\n\nNo legacy deck, modern package, or test files were modified — only the new plan document was added, as required. This PR is a draft proposal; approval of the plan is not approval of any code change.","branch":"plan/orbprp-modernization","title":"Modernization plan for ORBPRP"},"name":"create_pull_request"}}}
